cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Armilla Astrolabe: a digital abacus"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
abstract: "A residue-number-system digital abacus for CPUs. Rings precompute answers and a centre pulls them into SIMD: an exact ternary AI engine (5-trit codes at 1.6 bits per weight, AVX-512 and AVX2), exact f16 forward and backward passes via an evolved Gelosia lattice, bit-identical training across harnesses, a three-diamond multi-core unit, and RNS Montgomery modular exponentiation with AVX-512 IFMA that is faster than GMP powmod_sec at 2,048-16,384 bits on one core, with a fixed-base comb. Every result is measured and exact; failures are reported. Published as defensive prior art."
authors:
  - family-names: "De Santiago"
    given-names: "Juan Carlos"
license:
  - PolyForm-Small-Business-1.0.0
  - PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
keywords: [residue number system, chinese remainder theorem, lattice multiplication, gelosia, montgomery multiplication, carry-free arithmetic]
